I go to the reception desk.
A man is there.
I say to him, "Hello, brother."
"Hello madam, how can I help you?" he asks.
"I want to play badminton this evening," I tell him.
"I am new here."
"No problem madam, you can play here as a guest," bhaiya says.
"The fee for one day is two hundred rupees."
"Okay," I say.
"I do not have my own racket in Mumbai."
"Can I rent a racket here?" I ask.
"Yes madam, you can rent a racket," he says.
"The rent for the racket is fifty rupees."
Bhaiya gives me a racket.
I take the racket in my hand.
Its weight is perfectly fine.
I can play well with this racket.
I give bhaiya two hundred and fifty rupees.
Now I am ready to play.
